+#ifndef MOD_OLLAMA_CHAT_PVP_H
+#define MOD_OLLAMA_CHAT_PVP_H
+
+// --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// PvP appreciation / friendship subsystem.
+//
+// When someone fights well alongside random bots against the enemy faction --
+// and especially when they SAVE a bot that was about to die -- the nearby
+// friendly bots come to respect them: sentiment rises, they record a memory of
+// the moment, and (personality permitting) one reacts in voice. An unprovoked
+// GANK of a much-lower-level foe does the opposite: witnesses lose respect.
+// This applies whether the killer is a REAL player or another bot -- bots judge
+// each other's PvP conduct too, which quietly shapes who wants to guild with
+// whom. Because rising respect already gates guild invites, quest help and gear
+// gives elsewhere, honorable PvP organically earns friendship and guild spots.
+//
+// Two things are separated deliberately: RESPECT (sentiment) + memory ALWAYS
+// update; the spoken line is a CHANCE scaled by the bot's personality
+// talkativeness (chatty types pipe up, quiet ones stay silent) and only fires
+// when a real player is close enough to hear it -- so bot-vs-bot fights never
+// wake the LLM. Every line is generated by the model from explicit fight
+// context; nothing is hardcoded dialogue.
+//
+// Self-contained (all state + helpers local to the .cpp); reuses the existing
+// sentiment (NudgeSentimentPair), memory (RecordMemoryForPair), personality
+// (GetPersonalityReplyChanceMultiplier) and speak (OllamaChat_SpeakSituation)
+// machinery. Registered from Addmod_ollama_chatScripts() in
+// mod-ollama-chat_main.cpp.
+// --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+// Registration entry point. Call from Addmod_ollama_chatScripts().
+void AddSC_mod_ollama_chat_pvp();
+
+#endif // MOD_OLLAMA_CHAT_PVP_H
